| `http_client` has no validation pass. A field the particle does not carry is
| null, exactly as `.field` reads an absent member, and a url that cannot be
| fetched is simply a request that fails — so the message comes from
| attempting the request rather than from a guard refusing to try.
|
| Replaces fail_net_missing_url and fail_net_header_not_string (2026-08-28,
| docs/todo/errors-as-particles.md). Needs no network: nothing here gets
| far enough to open a socket except the refused one on port 1.
link "native_modules/http_client.so" as http

| No url at all: the request stage rejects an empty one, and says so.
emit Get {} to http get a
assert not a.ok
assert a.status = 0

| A url that is not a String is rendered rather than refused, so the
| message names what was actually asked for.
emit Get { url = 42 } to http get b
assert not b.ok

| A non-String header value is rendered too — `"X-Count" = 3` sends `3`,
| which is plainly what the caller meant. The request itself still fails,
| because nothing is listening on port 1.
emit Get { url = "http://127.0.0.1:1/", headers = { "X-Count" = 3 } } to http get c
assert not c.ok
assert c.status = 0

| A non-positive timeout falls back to the default instead of refusing —
| and, more to the point, instead of panicking inside Duration.
emit Get { url = "http://127.0.0.1:1/", timeout_seconds = -1 } to http get d
assert not d.ok
